Here's an interesting difference between the runs that reproduced the issue and the ones that didn't.

When the issue is reproduced, the nodes that we're not affected jump from `"term":2` to `"term":102` (on `node1` and `node2`) , so they presumably get the term data from the affected `node0`.

```
Running with 10000ms latency on node0
[...]
raft_status after 3 iterations:
Check raft
{"url":"http://localhost:6333","status":"ok","raft_info":{"term":95,"commit":141,"pending_operations":0,"leader":0,"role":"Candidate","is_voter":<nick>}}
{"url":"http://localhost:6343","status":"ok","raft_info":{"term":2,"commit":152,"pending_operations":0,"leader":3010363724257094,"role":"Follower","is_voter":<nick>}}
{"url":"http://localhost:6353","status":"ok","raft_info":{"term":2,"commit":152,"pending_operations":0,"leader":3010363724257094,"role":"Leader","is_voter":<nick>}}
Running with 10ms latency on node0
[...]
raft_status after 1 iterations:
Check raft
{"url":"http://localhost:6333","status":"ok","raft_info":{"term":102,"commit":142,"pending_operations":0,"leader":3010363724257094,"role":"Follower","is_voter":<nick>}}
{"url":"http://localhost:6343","status":"ok","raft_info":{"term":102,"commit":158,"pending_operations":0,"leader":3010363724257094,"role":"Follower","is_voter":<nick>}}
{"url":"http://localhost:6353","status":"ok","raft_info":{"term":102,"commit":158,"pending_operations":0,"leader":3010363724257094,"role":"Leader","is_voter":<nick>}}
Delete collection
```

When the issue is NOT reproduced, the affected node gets its term data from the non-affected nodes (`"term":1` to `"term":2` on `node0`).

```
